{{Quote|Ex-squeeze me, but da most safest place t'would be Gunga city. 'Tis where I grew up. 'Tis a hidden city.|[[Jar Jar Binks]]|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
'''Otoh Gunga''', also known as simply '''Gungan City''' or '''Gunga City''', was a [[Gungan]] [[city]] located beneath the surface of [[Lake Paonga]] on the [[planet]] of [[Naboo]]. It was originally built by the Gungans in order to avoid contact with their surface-dwelling Naboo neighbors. When the [[Trade Federation]] [[Battle of Naboo|invaded]] Naboo, their [[Army|armies]] stormed the [[swamp]]s, forcing the Gungans to [[Attack on Otoh Gunga|abandon]] the city.

==Description==
{{Quote|I'm going to Otoh Gunga. Their technology is so different from ours, and I want to see how it affects their art.|[[Eirtaé]]|<ref name="Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Gungan_society.png|thumb|left|270px|The interior of Otoh Gunga]]
Otoh Gunga was a prominent [[Gungan]] [[city]] situated in the [[water]]s of [[Lake Paonga]] on the [[planet]] [[Naboo]]. Its bubble-like buildings were in fact hydrostatic [[force field]]s that contained breathable atmospheres for their occupiers, and had special portals that allowed its inhabitants to enter and exit. Since the Gungans actually grew the building material of their cities from the natural [[plasma]] of Naboo and [[bubble wort extract]], the structure of Otoh Gunga was a hub and spoke network.<ref name="AbEverything" /> The bubbles, which housed around one million residents, were anchored to the lake floor by huge stone pillars. The designs of the buildings were inspired by [[fish]], fish [[egg]]s, aquatic [[plant]]s, and air bubbles.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

The city notably housed the [[Gungan High Council|High Council]], which ruled over the Gungans from the [[High Board Room]].<ref name="dbOG" /> It also contained a number of "invertebrate eateries" as well as an attraction called the City Bigspace, which was build by [[Boss]] [[Rugor Nass]]. The oldest part of the city is known as the Ancient Quarter.<ref name="CL 2016" />

==History==
{{Quote|My troops are in position to begin searching the swamps for these rumored underwater villages. They will not stay hidden for long.|[[OOM-9]], to [[Nute Gunray]]|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
The city was originally built by the Gungans in order to avoid contact with their surface-dwelling Naboo neighbors.<ref name="AbEverything" /> When the [[Trade Federation]] [[Battle of Naboo|invaded]] Naboo, their [[Army|armies]] stormed the [[swamp]]s, forcing the Gungans to [[Attack on Otoh Gunga|abandon]] Otoh Gunga.<ref name="SWE Gungans">{{SWE|groups|gungans|Gungans}}</ref>

[[File:Otoh_Gunga_TPM.png|thumb|right|260px|Qui-Gon, Obi-Wan, and Jar Jar visit Otoh Gunga]]
In [[28 BBY]], after leaving [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]]'s service following her last term as [[Monarch of Naboo|monarch]], the former [[Naboo Royal Handmaidens|handmaiden]] [[Eirtaé]] moved to Otoh Gunga wanting to see how their technology affected their art.<ref name="Queen's Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref>

In [[32 BBY]], the Gungan [[Jar Jar Binks]] was [[Exile (punishment)|banished]] from Otoh Gunga by Boss Nass after he crashed the Gungan leader's personal [[heyblibber]] [[submarine]].<ref name="Episode I" /> Following the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo]] shortly after, their [[Army|armies]] stormed the [[swamp]]s, forcing the Gungans to [[Attack on Otoh Gunga|abandon]] Otoh Gunga.<ref name="SWE Gungans">{{SWE|groups|gungans|Gungans}}</ref> [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] were sent to the planet by the [[Galactic Republic]]. There, they met the outcast Binks, who led them to Otoh Gunga at their behest despite his banishment. From there, the Jedi were granted a [[Tribubble bongo|bongo submarine]] and used the vessel to travel to the capital city of [[Theed]].<ref name="Episode I" />

Following the [[Invasions of Naboo]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[New Republic]] [[starfighter]] [[pilot]] [[Yendor Brethen|Yendor]] invited his fellow [[Corona Squadron]] mates to dine in Otoh Gunga. The city's residents were said to be able to produce a dessert that took at least four hominids to consume. This dessert was said to deliver one into a straight [[sugar]] coma. However, one of the pilots, [[Thane Kyrell]], elected not to join his mates because he was still mourning the loss of his former [[Imperial Academy]] [[Imperial cadet|classmate]] [[Ciena Ree]], whom he believed had perished during the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Otoh Gunga first appeared in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I" /> According to early storyboards of the film, Otoh Gunga was meant to be wiped out along with the Gungans prior to the Battle of Naboo. However, as genocide was judged to be too dark for the film, the story was adjusted.<ref name="SWS:TPT">''[[Star Wars Storyboards: The Prequel Trilogy]]''</ref>

